Contributions
Agentic System Design. We design a what-if outage analysis system with a single decision-making agent, deterministic analysis tools, a budget gate, and an append-only evidence context.
End-to-End Design Validation. We validate the design through a human-executed case study that follows the full investigation loop, from an initial what-if query to a four-class regional impact map.
Reusable Investigation Trace. We record every decision, tool call, and result as a reusable trace, providing the foundation for future agent skill learning.
Conclusion
Multi-Source Evidence Is Necessary. The case required the joint analysis of all three evidence sources to assess outage impact.
The Investigation Is Evidence-Driven. Decisions about where to search and how to allocate the analysis budget emerged from intermediate evidence rather than a fixed script.
Decision Automation Is the Next Step. The immediate next step is to automate the agent’s decision-making role in the investigation loop
